# 11. DAILY AND WEEKLY PROGRESS CALCULATIONS

Implement accurate, testable progress calculations.

Daily study goal progress:

Daily goal completion percentage =
Actual completed study minutes today / Target study minutes today × 100.

Weekly goal completion percentage =
Actual completed study minutes this week / Target study minutes this week × 100.

Task completion rate =
Number of completed tasks / Number of tasks due in the selected period × 100.

Flashcard accuracy =
Correct recall responses / Total answered review cards × 100.

Quiz accuracy =
Correct answers / Total questions answered × 100.

Handle division by zero safely. Display zero or "لا توجد بيانات كافية" when appropriate.

Clearly distinguish:
- Study time.
- Task completion.
- Learning progress.
- Quiz accuracy.
- Flashcard recall.

Do not combine these different measures into one misleading score.

Create daily, weekly, and monthly reports with:
- Total study hours.
- Average study hours per day.
- Study time by subject.
- Completed and overdue tasks.
- Flashcards reviewed.
- Quiz accuracy.
- Daily and weekly goal achievement.
- Comparison with the previous period.
- Best-performing subject based on available data.
- Suggested improvement for the next week.

The report must explain how each metric is calculated.

Do not label a student as successful or unsuccessful based only on hours studied.

